    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0425" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg329"/>

                <head>No. 257.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Turner to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Monrovia, Liberia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">Jan</hi>. 24, 1872</date>.
                        (Received Feb. 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to convey to the
                    Department a knowledge of the fact that his excellency President Roberts granted
                    the several members of the diplomatic corps now near the government of Liberia
                    an audience on the 15th day of January, 1872, at which time I received
                    satisfaction in being formally received or acknowledged by the President.
                    Inclosed please find copy of assurances offered by me upon that occasion.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. MILTON TURNER,</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d257-a1.xml" xpointer="d257-a1"/>
            </div>
